{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>For YHWH your Elohim, He is Elohei ha-Elohim.</b> The eternal over all the eternal beings that are separate from matter — their eternity flows from His eternity." "<b>And Adonei ha-Adonim.</b> The Guide of the guides — these being the spheres and their movers — whose governance is all directed toward achieving the end of His intention, in the manner of the particular angels relative to the principal ones." "<b>Ha-El ha-gadol.</b> There exists none equal to Him in the rank of His mode of existence." "<b>Ha-gibbor.</b> Who sustains all existence through His existence, as it says: וְאַתָּה מְחַיֶּה אֶת כֻּלָּם (Nehemiah 9:6)." "<b>Ve-hanora.</b> Who oversees to reward and to punish, in a manner worthy of being feared." "<b>Who does not lift the face.</b> In favor of a wicked son because of a righteous father, even though He prolongs His anger on account of the father's merit." "<b>And does not take a bribe.</b> He does not remove the punishment for a transgression on account of a commandment the sinner performed, as the Sages said: a commandment does not extinguish a transgression. All this is to teach you not to trust, if you sin, to escape punishment by any merit whatsoever — except through complete repentance."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:08.896773544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}